## Comparison of Image Classifiers for Environmental Microorganism Recognition

This notebook compares multiple deep learning models for the classification of environmental microorganism images. The models include various CNN-based and transformer-based architectures, trained and evaluated under consistent conditions.

The workflow includes:

- Loading and preprocessing of denoised and cropped image datasets
- Training and evaluation of multiple classifiers (Xception, ResNet-34, DenseNet-169, InceptionResNetV1, DeiT)
- Consistent use of metrics including accuracy, F1-score, and confusion matrix
- Visualization of model performance across classes
- Summary comparison of model strengths and weaknesses

The goal is to identify the most effective architecture for accurate multi-class classification of 21 microorganism types based on image data.

